# MPT Extension SDLC

This repository follows the SoftwareOne MPT extension SDLC. Cursor has no
versioned plugin marketplace, so this rule is the Cursor adapter: an always-on
pointer to the same skills and standards that the Claude and Codex plugins load.

## Where the source of truth lives

- `skills/` — reusable agent skills, one directory per skill, each with a
  `SKILL.md`. Skills are classified as `tool`, `task`, or `workflow`.
- `standards/` — normative engineering rules (commit messages, pull requests,
  Python coding, testing, documentation, dependencies). Follow these; do not
  restate or contradict them.
- `knowledge/` — reusable how-to guidance (build and checks, make targets,
  dependency management, migrations, backports).

When a consuming repository does not vendor these directories, read them from the
installed skills root (`~/.mpt-extension-skills/current`) or from the `main`
branch of `softwareone-platform/mpt-extension-skills`.

## Always-on conventions

- Commit messages: tag, Jira ID in the body, short imperative subject; follow
  `standards/commit-messages.md`.
- Pull requests: one commit per PR, Jira ID in the title, reviewable scope;
  follow `standards/pull-requests.md`.
- Validation: run the repository's required checks and tests before committing or
  opening a PR; see `knowledge/build-and-checks.md`.
- Jira lifecycle: move work to Done only after the reviewed PR is merged.

For any concrete SDLC step (start work, commit, open PR, handle review comments,
complete after merge), follow the matching `skills/mpt-ext-*/SKILL.md`.
